Samoa PHC 2021
Census Population characteristics

This Fact Sheet presents the indicators of the 2021 PHC
Page 3 Section on “Demographic and social characteristics of the population ” presents 8 indicators
Page 5
Fertility indicators measure the frequency of childbirth in a given population. Such measures can tell how 
fast the population of a given country or region would increase. Some of the most common methods have 
been applied to get better understanding of the fertility performance of the population relating to Current 
fertility, 
Page 6
Mortality is the state or condition of being subjected to death. Mortality data is useful in assessing the 
overall health of the population of a country. Information on mortality measures including; Crude death rate, 
Infant mortality rate, Under five mortality rate and Life expectancy
Page 7
“Education section includes indicators on four levels of education namely: Early Childhood Education (ECE) 
or commonly known as Kindergarten or Pre- School, Primary, Secondary, and higher education comprising 
of all the Post-Secondary/Tertiary education .It also shows the highest level of qualification achieved by the 
population 15yrs and over.
Page 9
Economic section of the population includes  key economic characteristics of population 15 years and over 
based on respondents main economic activities in the last 7 days reference period prior to the 2021 
census date. 
Page 11 Housing , land tenure and household amenities indicators are listed here
Page 12 “Water, sanitation and hygiene covers  indicators  on households main source of drinking water, sanitation 
facilities and the hygiene level used.
Page 13 Energy section covers indicators on energy used by the household for cookingand lighting .It also covers 
indicators on types of metered use by household for electricity.
Page  14 “Transportation section covers indicators on ownership of vehicles by households as well as the types of 
transportation usually used by the household members
Page  15
Communication and technology section covers indicators on ownership of different devices collected by 
census as well as the ownership of radios, television and the radios and television stations which are 
usually used by the households.
Pg 17 Labour Mobility where Regional seasonal workers indicators were listed 
Page 18 Transportation section listed indicators on the number of vehicles owned by households aswell as the main 
means of transportation usually used by households
